      "note": "State-pension-age adjustment (Comment 'DEF: Pension age adjustment - changes in earnings and pensions due to increase in the state pension age'; Type ben but a switch-type toggle). Its functions only *adjust input variables* for the SPA-rise counterfactual: for people below state pension age it subtracts the observed state pension (formula (-boact_s) into boact_s), swaps observed earnings/hours/ self-employment for imputed values (yem := yemiv, lhw00 := lhwiv00, yse := yseiv, output_add_var each), and re-derives lhw. It computes no distinct payable instrument \u2014 boact_s is written only to zero it out pre-SPA, not to pay a benefit. This is input-carrying (the InitVars pattern), not a scored surface; reclassified from the initial seed's in-scope guess (evidence: UK.xml UK_2026 PAA_uk function body).",
