      "note": "BEN: Child Benefit. The uk-child-benefit suite live-compares the composed UK Child Benefit pipeline (SSCBA 1992 s.141 with the SI 2006/965 reg.2 enhanced GBP 27.05 / other GBP 17.90 weekly rates, annualised over 52 weeks) against UKMOD's pre-charge Child Benefit on a single-parent grid (one/two/three children x 20k/70k/80k/90k straddling the HICBC taper), matching 12/12. The comparison bridges to UKMOD by summing paid bch_s and the separately-reported charge clawback bchrd_s (the HICBC, ITEPA 2003 s.681B-H, is not in the Axiom corpus \u2014 rulespec-uk#75 \u2014 so the netted pre-charge Child Benefit is the parity target). The ~0.27% 52-vs-52.14-weeks convention residual is inside tolerance; all cases recover the same statutory weekly rates. bch_s is the compared surface, so bch_uk is covered.",
