      "note": "BEN: Statutory Maternity Pay. The UKMOD Comment says \"(not simulated in the baseline)\", but the UK_2026 policy is switch=on and computes bmact_s from ordinary demographic/earnings inputs \u2014 female (dgn=0) with a newborn (dag<1, baby-months dmb), earnings above the SMP lower-earnings-limit ($SMPlel), working hours (liwwh>6), and previous earnings i_yempv_bmact \u2014 with the 90%/flat-rate SMP formula over i_durweeks_bmact2. No maternity-leave-spell column is required, so it IS comparable on synthetic HHoT cases. Kept in scope as a genuine uncovered surface (not excluded): Axiom has no SMP suite yet and rulespec-uk does not encode SMP (docs/uk-coverage-matrix.md). Next-wave worklist. (Distinct from the bfapl_be dataset-blocked case, whose activating leave column is genuinely absent from its schema.)",
