      "note": "State Pension (contributory). UKMOD does not compute the state pension from contribution records \u2014 its whole UK_2026 body is boact_s = boact00 * (SPSingle/SPSingle0): it takes the reported state- pension data input boact00 and applies an uprating factor. This is an uprating passthrough of a data input, computing no distinct entitlement from statute, so it is input-carrying, not a scored surface. Confirmed by the uk-pension-credit suite, whose live worker verifies \"the boact_uk policy only uprates the boact00 state-pension data input\" and feeds boact_s as an income-test input rather than a parity target. Reclassified from the initial seed's in-scope guess (evidence: UK.xml UK_2026 boact_uk body).",
